# ===========================================================================
# Ray Tracing
# ===========================================================================
option.ACCUMULATION_LENGTH = Refraction History Frames
option.ACCUMULATION_LENGTH.comment = Maximum reprojected history used by the refraction denoiser. MaxEnt reflection history is controlled separately below.

option.RAY_BOUNCES = Ray Bounces
option.RAY_BOUNCES.comment = Maximum surfaces visited by each camera path. More bounces preserve deep indirect light and transmission at a direct GPU cost.

option.PATH_GUIDING_STRENGTH = Path Guiding Strength
option.PATH_GUIDING_STRENGTH.comment = MaxEnt guiding strength for diffuse paths and the total MaxEnt+RIS guided probability for radiance-cache probes. Cache probes always retain at least 10% uniform-sphere sampling. Higher values can converge faster in stable scenes; excessive values can increase lag or variance after lighting changes.

option.RESTIR_GI_ENABLED = Biased Low-History ReSTIR GI Path-Guide Prewarm
option.RESTIR_GI_ENABLED.comment = While validated diffuse history is low, luminance-resamples directions and bounds their energy by the local mean to give MaxEnt a low-variance starting guide. The bias is cleared as history matures. Requires EON.
value.RESTIR_GI_ENABLED.1 = Enabled
value.RESTIR_GI_ENABLED.0 = Disabled

option.RESTIR_GI_SPATIAL_SAMPLES = Prewarm Spatial Samples
option.RESTIR_GI_SPATIAL_SAMPLES.comment = Number of current-frame neighbouring proposals considered per pixel. Candidates are buffer-only; just the selected shifted donor emits one geometry visibility ray.

option.RESTIR_GI_SPATIAL_RADIUS = Prewarm Spatial Radius
option.RESTIR_GI_SPATIAL_RADIUS.comment = Current-frame neighbour radius in pixels. Larger radii explore less correlated paths but more candidates fail the primary-plane compatibility test.

option.RESTIR_GI_VISIBILITY_MAX_DISTANCE = Prewarm Visibility Distance
option.RESTIR_GI_VISIBILITY_MAX_DISTANCE.comment = Maximum distance in blocks for spatial support rays. These rays test opaque triangle geometry only and skip alpha, transmission, textures and all closest-hit material evaluation. Lower values are faster but do not query blockers beyond the cap.

option.RESTIR_GI_HISTORY_FADE_START = Prewarm Fade Start
option.RESTIR_GI_HISTORY_FADE_START.comment = Keep full ReSTIR bootstrap contribution below this geometrically validated previous-frame diffuse history length.

option.RESTIR_GI_HISTORY_FADE_END = Prewarm Fade End
option.RESTIR_GI_HISTORY_FADE_END.comment = Clear the biased prewarm signal and switch fully to the canonical MaxEnt path sample at this diffuse history length. Stable pixels skip candidate processing and visibility rays.

option.RESTIR_GI_NORMAL_COS = Prewarm Normal Cosine
option.RESTIR_GI_NORMAL_COS.comment = Minimum geometry-normal cosine for a neighbour to join the proposal set. Raise it to isolate block faces more aggressively and reduce biased prewarm leakage across sharp corners.

option.RESTIR_GI_PLANE_DISTANCE = Prewarm Plane Distance
option.RESTIR_GI_PLANE_DISTANCE.comment = Maximum neighbour distance from the target tangent plane in blocks. Lower values reject adjacent block faces and steps more aggressively.

option.SUN_PATH_ROTATION = Sun Path Rotation
option.SUN_PATH_ROTATION.comment = Tilts the apparent sun and moon path around the world X axis like latitude. This changes lighting direction, not day length. 30° is the spring clear-sky calibration reference for the atmosphere.

option.END_SKYBOX = End Skybox
option.END_SKYBOX.comment = Selects the custom rune-ring and nebula sky in the End. Disabling it uses the cheaper atmospheric fallback.
value.END_SKYBOX.1 = Rune Rings + Nebula
value.END_SKYBOX.0 = Atmospheric Scatter

option.FIREFLY_SUPPRESSION_MULTIPLIER = Firefly Suppression
option.FIREFLY_SUPPRESSION_MULTIPLIER.comment = Per-sample brightness cap multiplier (× average exposure). Lower values clamp bright outlier samples more aggressively, reducing fireflies but potentially darkening specular highlights.

option.GI_CLAMP_MAX = GI Hard Clamp
option.GI_CLAMP_MAX.comment = Hard ceiling on indirect lighting (per-channel) before MaxEnt encoding. Prevents individual path outliers from destabilising the light-field history. Higher values give more headroom for bright indirect light; lower values suppress extreme fireflies more aggressively.

option.PATHGUIDE_SPATIAL_RADIUS = Path Guide Spatial Radius
option.PATHGUIDE_SPATIAL_RADIUS.comment = Poisson disk sampling radius (pixels) for the path-guide ReSTIR reservoir. Higher values probe farther neighbours for more diverse candidates but increase incoherent memory access.

option.PATHGUIDE_MAX_TEMPORAL_M = Path Guide Max Temporal M
option.PATHGUIDE_MAX_TEMPORAL_M.comment = Maximum effective sample count carried forward by the path-guide ReSTIR temporal reservoir. Limits how many past samples influence the current guide. Higher values retain more history but respond more slowly to lighting changes.

# ===========================================================================
# Material
# ===========================================================================
option.EON_ENABLED = EON Rough Diffuse
option.EON_ENABLED.comment = Uses the energy-preserving Oren--Nayar diffuse model with MaxEnt integration. This improves rough-surface response and white-furnace energy conservation at a higher shader cost.
value.EON_ENABLED.1 = Enabled
value.EON_ENABLED.0 = Disabled (Legacy)

option.REFRACTIVE_INDEX = Water IOR
option.REFRACTIVE_INDEX.comment = Index of refraction used only by water. Higher values bend transmitted rays more strongly and increase grazing reflection.

option.GLASS_REFRACTIVE_INDEX = Glass IOR
option.GLASS_REFRACTIVE_INDEX.comment = Index of refraction used by glass and glass panes. It is evaluated independently from water throughout the path; ice uses its physical 1.31 value.

option.MAX_WETNESS = Max Wetness
option.MAX_WETNESS.comment = Maximum rain-induced wetness applied to materials. Higher values make porous surfaces darker and all wet surfaces smoother without changing substrate F0.

# ===========================================================================
# Parallax Occlusion Mapping
# ===========================================================================
option.POM_ENABLED = Parallax Mapping
option.POM_ENABLED.comment = Enables parallax occlusion mapping on the camera-visible surface. It improves apparent depth in supported textures at extra texture-sampling cost.
value.POM_ENABLED.1 = On
value.POM_ENABLED.0 = Off

option.POM_STEPS = POM Ray Steps
option.POM_STEPS.comment = Number of linear ray-marching steps for parallax occlusion mapping. Higher values produce sharper displacement at higher GPU cost. Lower values are faster but can miss fine surface detail.

option.POM_DEPTH = POM Depth Scale
option.POM_DEPTH.comment = Maximum apparent depth of surface displacement in world units. Higher values make bumps and crevices appear deeper. The visual effect depends on the underlying height-map texture.

option.BINARY_SEARCH_STEPS = POM Refinement Steps
option.BINARY_SEARCH_STEPS.comment = Binary search refinement iterations after the linear ray march. Higher values yield more precise surface intersection and sharper occlusion edges. Set to 0 to disable refinement (faster, softer results).

# ===========================================================================
# Sparse Radiance Cache
# ===========================================================================
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_MAX_ALLOCATIONS_PER_FRAME = New Bricks per Frame
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_MAX_ALLOCATIONS_PER_FRAME.comment = Limits physical brick allocations per frame. Lower values reduce frame-time spikes; higher values make newly visible geometry converge faster.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_RESIDENT_HYSTERESIS_BUCKETS = Resident Hysteresis
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_RESIDENT_HYSTERESIS_BUCKETS.comment = Gives resident bricks a priority advantage measured in 4-block distance buckets. Higher values improve stability but keep old bricks longer.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_MARK_TILE_SIZE = Request Sampling Tile
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_MARK_TILE_SIZE.comment = Submits one geometry request sample per NxN screen tile. Smaller tiles improve coverage but execute more atomic request operations.
value.RADIANCE_CACHE_MARK_TILE_SIZE.4 = 4x4 Fine
value.RADIANCE_CACHE_MARK_TILE_SIZE.8 = 8x8 Balanced
value.RADIANCE_CACHE_MARK_TILE_SIZE.16 = 16x16 Fast

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_ROUGH_SPECULAR_THRESHOLD = Rough Specular Threshold
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_ROUGH_SPECULAR_THRESHOLD.comment = Minimum PSR-style cascaded roughness for terminating a secondary specular path into the radiance cache. Lower values are faster; higher values retain sharper reflections.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_DIFFUSE_MIN_BOUNCE = Diffuse Cache Start Bounce
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_DIFFUSE_MIN_BOUNCE.comment = First path bounce allowed to terminate a diffuse path into the radiance cache. Bounce 1 is the camera-visible surface. Higher values reduce cache artifacts but trace more rays.

option.VOXEL_SIZE = Cache Voxel Size
option.VOXEL_SIZE.comment = Edge length of a single radiance-cache voxel in world units. Smaller voxels increase spatial precision and capture finer lighting detail, but require more bricks and memory to cover the same volume.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_MAX_HIST = Cache RIS Max M
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_MAX_HIST.comment = Maximum effective candidate count retained by each voxel's temporal RIS reservoir. Higher values reuse important bright samples longer; lower values react faster when lighting or geometry changes.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_FILTER_MAX_HIST = Cache Smoothing Frames
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_FILTER_MAX_HIST.comment = Temporal sample count used to accumulate the cache's directional MaxEnt moments directly. Higher values reduce directional and energy variance; lower values react faster and reduce lighting trails. Lighting, recursive feedback and cache path guiding all use this result.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_UPDATE_PERIOD = Cache Update Period
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_UPDATE_PERIOD.comment = Number of frames between update rays for resident cache voxels. Newly allocated bricks are still fully initialized on their birth frame. A value of 4 reduces steady-state cache rays and Resolve work by about 75%; higher values are faster but respond and converge more slowly.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_RIS_GUIDING_STRENGTH = Cache RIS Guide Share
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_RIS_GUIDING_STRENGTH.comment = Maximum fraction of a cache probe's total guided probability assigned to the temporal RIS direction proposal. It reaches this share only when the reservoir agrees with the stable MaxEnt field in direction and energy and has sufficient history. 0 disables RIS guiding.

option.RADIANCE_CACHE_RIS_GUIDING_KAPPA = Cache RIS Guide Sharpness
option.RADIANCE_CACHE_RIS_GUIDING_KAPPA.comment = Concentration of the continuous sampling lobe around the RIS-selected direction. Higher values can find compact lights faster but are more sensitive to stale or imprecise directions; lower values are more robust.

# ===========================================================================
# Shared MaxEnt Temporal Response
# ===========================================================================
option.MAXENT_TEMPORAL_RESPONSE_DISTANCE_SCALE = Moment-distance Response Scale
option.MAXENT_TEMPORAL_RESPONSE_DISTANCE_SCALE.comment = Shared by diffuse and specular temporal accumulation. It scales squared moment distance relative to the combined estimator variance. Higher values give the current frame more weight for the same difference and reject history more aggressively.

# ===========================================================================
# MaxEnt Diffuse Temporal
# ===========================================================================
option.MAXENT_DIFFUSE_TEMPORAL_DEPTH_SCALE = Reprojection Depth Scale
option.MAXENT_DIFFUSE_TEMPORAL_DEPTH_SCALE.comment = Scales the depth half-extent of the temporal reprojection footprint trapezoid. Higher values accept history samples that are farther off the reconstructed surface plane, reducing resets but potentially leaking across thin geometry.

option.MAXENT_DIFFUSE_TEMPORAL_REPROJECTION_RADIUS = Diffuse Reprojection Radius
option.MAXENT_DIFFUSE_TEMPORAL_REPROJECTION_RADIUS.comment = Diffuse temporal footprint radius in pixels. Larger values accept wider path reprojection motion.

# ===========================================================================
# MaxEnt Specular Temporal
# ===========================================================================
option.MAXENT_SPECULAR_TEMPORAL_DISOCCLUSION_THRESHOLD = Disocclusion Threshold
option.MAXENT_SPECULAR_TEMPORAL_DISOCCLUSION_THRESHOLD.comment = Relative plane-distance tolerance for reprojected surfaces. Lower values reject more history; higher values can leak history across thin geometry.

option.MAXENT_SPECULAR_TEMPORAL_LOBE_FRACTION = Lobe Fraction
option.MAXENT_SPECULAR_TEMPORAL_LOBE_FRACTION.comment = Portion of the GGX lobe accepted during temporal reprojection. Lower values reject more history around view-dependent reflection changes.

option.MAXENT_SPECULAR_TEMPORAL_REPROJECTION_RADIUS = Specular Reprojection Radius
option.MAXENT_SPECULAR_TEMPORAL_REPROJECTION_RADIUS.comment = Specular temporal footprint radius in pixels. Larger values accept wider reflection reprojection motion.






# ===========================================================================
# MaxEnt Variance Preparation
# ===========================================================================
option.MAXENT_VARIANCE_KERNEL_SIGMA = Kernel Sigma
option.MAXENT_VARIANCE_KERNEL_SIGMA.comment = Shared diffuse/specular Gaussian kernel width for short-history MaxEnt variance pooling. Higher values trade edge precision for a more stable estimate.

option.MAXENT_VARIANCE_HISTORY_BEGIN = Transition Begin Samples
option.MAXENT_VARIANCE_HISTORY_BEGIN.comment = Shared diffuse/specular effective sample count at which the spatial-to-temporal estimator-variance transition begins.

option.MAXENT_VARIANCE_HISTORY_END = Transition End Samples
option.MAXENT_VARIANCE_HISTORY_END.comment = Shared diffuse/specular effective sample count at which temporal estimator variance is fully trusted and large-kernel pooling is skipped.

# ===========================================================================
# MaxEnt Spatial Filter
# ===========================================================================
option.MAXENT_SPATIAL_PLANE_DISTANCE_TOLERANCE = Plane-distance Tolerance
option.MAXENT_SPATIAL_PLANE_DISTANCE_TOLERANCE.comment = Relative projected plane-depth tolerance used by MaxEnt virtual-image rejection, refraction, and path-guide spatial tests. Higher values permit more cross-plane filtering.

option.MAXENT_SPATIAL_DIFFUSE_LIGHT_FIELD_SENSITIVITY = Diffuse Light-field Sensitivity
option.MAXENT_SPATIAL_DIFFUSE_LIGHT_FIELD_SENSITIVITY.comment = Variance-normalized diffuse moment-space rejection strength. Higher values preserve more light-field contrast; lower values smooth more.

option.MAXENT_SPATIAL_SPECULAR_LIGHT_FIELD_SENSITIVITY = Specular Light-field Sensitivity
option.MAXENT_SPATIAL_SPECULAR_LIGHT_FIELD_SENSITIVITY.comment = Variance-normalized specular moment-space rejection strength. Higher values preserve more reflection contrast; lower values smooth more.

# ===========================================================================
# Bloom
# ===========================================================================
option.CAMERA_VIGNETTE_STRENGTH = Camera Vignette Strength
option.CAMERA_VIGNETTE_STRENGTH.comment = Mixes RT-projection and FOV-aware cos^4 lens falloff into the HDR scene before bloom. Zero disables it; one applies the ideal cos^4 law.

option.BLOOM_MIX = Bloom Strength
option.BLOOM_MIX.comment = Fraction of the final image contributed by bloom. Zero disables bloom blending; high values can wash out local contrast.
option.BLOOM_DIFFUSION_SCALE = Bloom Diffusion Scale
option.BLOOM_DIFFUSION_SCALE.comment = Multiplies the Gaussian scattering radius of all RGB channels while preserving their wavelength ratios. Higher values produce a broader lens-scattering halo.
option.BLOOM_CHROMATIC_SCATTER = Lens Wavelength Scattering
option.BLOOM_CHROMATIC_SCATTER.comment = Sets the small-particle Rayleigh fraction of lens-scattering power. Zero approximates wavelength-independent large-particle forward scatter; one is the pure-Rayleigh upper limit. The variance-domain blend uses representative 611/549/464 nm RGB wavelengths; pure Rayleigh gives sigma ratios of approximately 0.807, 1.000 and 1.400.

# ===========================================================================
# Exposure & Display
# ===========================================================================
option.DISPLAY_MAX_LUMINANCE = Display Peak Luminance
option.DISPLAY_MAX_LUMINANCE.comment = Approximate display peak brightness in nits, used to scale HDR exposure. Set this near the sustained peak brightness of your display.

option.DISPLAY_PAPER_WHITE_LUMINANCE = sRGB Paper White Luminance
option.DISPLAY_PAPER_WHITE_LUMINANCE.comment = Target brightness of ordinary diffuse white relative to the display range. Lower values leave more highlight headroom and make exposure appear brighter.

option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_OUTLIER_TOLERANCE = Auto-Exposure Outlier Tolerance
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE_OUTLIER_TOLERANCE.comment = Controls the width of soft outlier weighting in log-luminance space. Lower values reject isolated bright and dark samples more aggressively; higher values let them influence exposure more strongly.

option.EXPOSURE_CURVE_K = Exposure Curve
option.EXPOSURE_CURVE_K.comment = Compresses highlights before tone mapping. Zero disables the curve; higher values retain more bright detail but reduce highlight contrast.

option.PUPIL_MIN_DIAMETER_MM = Minimum Pupil Diameter
option.PUPIL_MIN_DIAMETER_MM.comment = Smallest pupil diameter in bright conditions, in millimetres. It limits fast optical adaptation; slower retinal/neural adaptation still supplies the remaining exposure range, so this is not used as a total-exposure floor. A typical adult range is approximately 2–4 mm.

option.PUPIL_MAX_DIAMETER_MM = Maximum Pupil Diameter
option.PUPIL_MAX_DIAMETER_MM.comment = Largest pupil diameter in dark conditions, in millimetres. It limits fast optical adaptation while slower retinal/neural adaptation continues in dark scenes. A typical adult range is approximately 6–8 mm; a 4 mm pupil represents 1x optical exposure.

# ===========================================================================
# Advanced
# ===========================================================================
option.VPROJDIST_SKY = Sky Virtual Distance
option.VPROJDIST_SKY.comment = Virtual projected distance (meters) assigned to sky pixels in the specular and refraction denoisers. Used to tag infinity hits so the denoiser can identify sky regions. Rarely needs adjustment.

# ===========================================================================
# Debug
# ===========================================================================
option.DEBUG_RT_FORCE_GEOMETRY_NORMAL = RT Geometry Normals Only
option.DEBUG_RT_FORCE_GEOMETRY_NORMAL.comment = Replaces normal-mapped shading normals with face-forward triangle geometry normals in every RT material evaluation and disables RT parallax occlusion mapping. Rasterized G-buffer materials are unchanged.
value.DEBUG_RT_FORCE_GEOMETRY_NORMAL.1 = On
value.DEBUG_RT_FORCE_GEOMETRY_NORMAL.0 = Off

option.DEBUG_VIEW = Categorized Debug View
option.DEBUG_VIEW.comment = Grouped by output, material, denoiser, refraction, cache, and motion. Scalar heat maps generally use blue for low, red for high, and magenta for invalid data.
